	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  REFCURSOR et PHP]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=4080#p4080"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Si cela peut aider d&#039;autres personnes :</p><p>function test_refcursor()<br />{<br />&#160; pg_query(&quot;begin&quot;);<br />&#160; $res1 = pg_query(&quot;SELECT fcurs()&quot;);<br />&#160; if ($res1!==false) {<br />&#160; &#160; list($cname) = pg_fetch_array($res1);<br />&#160; &#160; $res2 = pg_query(&quot;FETCH ALL IN \&quot;&quot; . $cname . &quot;\&quot;&quot;);<br />&#160; &#160; if ($res2!==false) {<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; $all = pg_fetch_all($res2);<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; print_r($all);<br />&#160; &#160; }<br />&#160; }<br />&#160; pg_query(&quot;commit&quot;);<br />}</p><p>Solution proposée par Estofilo sur Developpez.com</p>]]></content>
